WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.467
Pat the salmon dry on a separate prep tray. Season with salt and pepper. Have the measured sauce ingredients ready.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:20.600
Sear salmon in olive oil until golden, then turn carefully. Continue until the thickest part reaches 145°F. Transfer to a warm plate.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:27.933
Lower the heat. Add butter and minced shallot to the skillet and cook until the shallot softens.

00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:35.733
Add the broth and gently scrape up browned bits. Simmer until the liquid reduces by about half.

00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:42.478
Stir in heavy cream and lemon juice. Simmer gently until the sauce lightly thickens.

00:00:42.478 --> 00:00:50.478
Spoon lemon cream sauce onto warm plates. Add the fully cooked salmon and finish with chopped parsley.
